  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Tuesday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Upper level trof continues to deepen as\nit moves south thru British Columbia. Latest numerical model\nsolutions depict a cut off low forming over Oregon tonight, with\nthe low residing over NorCal thru Thursday before ejecting east.\nThis will produce elevated winds, especially across central Nevada\nand White Pine County, each afternoon thru Thursday. South-\nsouthwesterly gusts will be 25 to 35 MPH, reaching around 45 MPH\nacross the high terrain. Patchy blowing dust can be expected.\nSignificant precipitation will not be present, though locations \nalong the Idaho and Oregon borders may experience a brief light \nrain shower or two under the influence of the upper low, \nespecially the northwest quadrant of Humboldt County. \nConcurrently, significant moisture across Utah, thanks to a \nnortherly push of subtropical moisture from the desert southwest, \nwill spill into portions of Nevada and provide a low chance for a\nbrief shower or dry thunderstorm across the eastern half of White\nPine County, primarily over the Snake Range. Temperatures across \nnorthern Nevada cool several degrees Thursday as the low and \nassociated cooler air mass influence the region. \n\nTemperatures gradually warm thru the weekend with a return to\ndaytime highs in the upper 70s to mid 80s across the valleys by\nSunday. Weather looks to be dry though a low chance (10%) for rain\nshowers across central Nevada will be present early next week as a\nweak Pacific low pressure system moves into Central California\nfrom the west. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: There is high confidence in\nbreezy to strong south-southwesterly winds each afternoon thru\nThursday as an upper level trof passes thru the western U.S.\n\nModerate confidence in a 10% to 15% chance for isolated showers \nWednesday thru Thursday for far northern Nevada, as well as \neastern White Pine County where a dry thunderstorm or two may also\nbe present. \n\nLow confidence in a 10% chance for light rain across central\nNevada early next week.",
